IMPORT prelude

-- Wills Act 2000 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in plain days ("dies within 30 days after the death of the
-- testator", s 34(1); "survive the testator for 30 days", s 40(1); "until 30 days after his or her death", s 55(1)) and in
-- months ("within 6 months after the date of the death of the testator", s 27(2)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word reprint REPW007 of the Wills Act
-- 2000 (NT), as in force at 1 January 2022, not an official version. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned
-- by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October
-- 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Wills Act 2000`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- The number of days in a calendar month.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months after a day. The day itself is excluded (the Interpretation Act 1978
-- (NT), a borrowed rule, not deposited), so the period ends on the same day-number n months later; where that month is
-- shorter, on its last day (31 August + 6 months ends 28 or 29 February). Fork F7 in NOTES.md.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day` `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the start` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the start` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the month index` MEANS `the count` MODULO 12
        `the year` MEANS (`the count` MINUS `the month index`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `the month` MEANS `the month index` PLUS 1
        `the day` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
            THEN `the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`
